🧩 1. What is Amazon EBS?

Amazon EBS (Elastic Block Store) provides persistent block storage volumes for EC2 instances.

Think of it like an external hard drive for your EC2.

It persists even after instance termination (if you choose so).

It’s highly available and replicated within an AZ.

⚙️ Key Points:
Feature	Description
Type	Block storage (like HDD/SSD)
Scope	Works within the same Availability Zone
Durability	Replicated automatically within AZ
Attach	You can attach/detach anytime
Backup	Snapshots stored in S3
Encryption	Built-in at rest + in transit
Use Cases	Databases, Boot volumes, File systems, Big data apps
🧠 EBS vs Instance Store
Feature	EBS Volume	Instance Store
Persistence	Data persists after stop/restart	Data lost after stop/terminate
Attachment	Can be attached/detached	Fixed to instance
Backup	Supports Snapshots	No backup possible
Performance	SSD/HDD options	Very high performance (temporary)
Cost	Pay for storage	Included with instance
Use Case	Databases, long-term storage	Temporary cache, buffer data
🪜 2. Create First Elastic Block Store Volume
Step-by-Step:

Go to EC2 → Elastic Block Store → Volumes

Click Create Volume

Volume type: gp3 (General Purpose SSD)

Size: 8 GiB

Availability Zone: us-east-1a

Click Create Volume

Select the volume → Actions → Attach Volume

Choose an EC2 Instance in the same AZ

Note device name: /dev/xvdf

Connect to EC2:
lsblk


You’ll see /dev/xvdf (unmounted).

Format & Mount EBS Volume:
sudo mkfs -t ext4 /dev/xvdf
sudo mkdir /data
sudo mount /dev/xvdf /data


Verify:

df -h


💡 Now your EBS volume is ready for use!

🔁 3. Detach an EBS Volume and Attach to Another EC2
Steps:

Stop the first EC2 instance.

Go to EC2 → Volumes → Select volume → Detach Volume.

Once detached → Attach it to another EC2 (same AZ).

On the new instance:

sudo mkdir /newdata
sudo mount /dev/xvdf /newdata


✅ You’ve migrated your volume data successfully.

📏 4. Resize EBS Volume and File System

You can increase the size or change the volume type without downtime.

Steps:

Go to EC2 → Volumes → Modify Volume

Increase size (e.g., 8 GB → 20 GB)

Wait for modification → state = optimizing

Then inside EC2:

sudo growpart /dev/xvdf 1
sudo resize2fs /dev/xvdf


✅ Volume resized successfully.

🧱 5. Resize Root EBS Volume

When you launch EC2, root EBS (e.g., /dev/xvda) may be small.

To resize:

Stop instance.

Go to Volumes → Modify Volume → Increase Size.

Start instance again.

Inside instance:

sudo growpart /dev/xvda 1
sudo resize2fs /dev/xvda1


✅ Root filesystem now uses full disk.

🔗 6. Attach One EBS Volume to Multiple EC2 Instances

⚠️ Normally, EBS can attach to one EC2 at a time.
But EBS Multi-Attach (io1/io2) allows multiple EC2s in the same AZ to access one volume concurrently.

Used in:

Clustered databases (Oracle RAC)

Shared storage systems

Requirements:

Volume type: io1 or io2

Same AZ

EC2 instances with Nitro system

⚙️ 7. EBS Volume Types
Type	Description	Use Case
gp3	General Purpose SSD (3,000 IOPS baseline)	Default for most workloads
gp2	Older SSD (IOPS linked to size)	Legacy workloads
io1 / io2	Provisioned IOPS SSD	Databases, latency-sensitive
st1	Throughput optimized HDD	Big data, log processing
sc1	Cold HDD	Infrequent access data, backups

💡 Best Practice:
Use gp3 for general workloads → cheap + consistent performance.

🧩 8. Snapshot Overview

A Snapshot is a point-in-time backup of your EBS volume stored in S3.

Incremental (only changed blocks are saved)

Can restore to new volume

Can copy across regions/accounts

📸 9. Create First Snapshot
Steps:

Go to EC2 → Volumes

Select volume → Actions → Create Snapshot

Add description → “Backup before upgrade”

Snapshot stored in EC2 → Snapshots

To restore:

Actions → Create Volume from Snapshot

⚙️ 10. Automate EBS Backups with Lifecycle Manager

EBS Lifecycle Manager automates snapshot creation & deletion.

Steps:

Go to EC2 → Lifecycle Manager → Create Policy

Select resource type: Volume

Define:

Schedule: daily/weekly

Retain snapshots for 7 days

Create policy ✅

💡 Automatically keeps your backups clean & up to date.

🗑 11. Snapshot and AMI Recycle Bin

AWS offers Recycle Bin for accidental snapshot or AMI deletion recovery.

You can define retention rules.

Deleted resources stay recoverable for a set period.

🌍 12. Copy Snapshot Across Regions / Accounts

Used for disaster recovery or migration.

Steps:

Select Snapshot → Actions → Copy Snapshot

Choose:

Destination Region

Encryption (optional)

Click Copy ✅

💡 You can also share snapshots with another AWS account.

🔐 13. Encrypt EBS Volumes

Encryption is AES-256 and handled by AWS KMS.

Action	Encrypted Automatically
Create new EBS volume	✅
Create snapshot from encrypted volume	✅
Copy encrypted snapshot	✅
Restore from encrypted snapshot	✅

💡 You can also encrypt an unencrypted volume by:

Taking snapshot → copying snapshot with encryption → creating new encrypted volume.

🧹 14. Delete EBS Volume / Snapshot
Delete EBS Volume:

Detach from EC2

Select → Actions → Delete Volume

Delete Snapshot:

EC2 → Snapshots → Select → Delete Snapshot

💡 Tip: Use Lifecycle Manager for automatic cleanup.

🧠 15. Interview Questions – Amazon EBS
❓ Question	💡 Answer
What is EBS?	Persistent block storage for EC2 instances.
Difference between EBS & Instance Store?	EBS = persistent, Instance Store = temporary.
Can you attach one EBS volume to multiple EC2s?	Only io1/io2 with Multi-Attach in same AZ.
What is a Snapshot?	Point-in-time backup of EBS volume.
Where are Snapshots stored?	In S3 (managed by AWS).
Are Snapshots incremental?	Yes, only changed blocks saved.
How do you restore a volume?	Create Volume from Snapshot.
What is EBS Lifecycle Manager?	Automates snapshot backups and cleanup.
What happens if I encrypt a volume?	Data is encrypted at rest and in transit.
What is gp3?	General-purpose SSD with independent IOPS.
Difference between gp2 & gp3?	gp3 has fixed IOPS (3000) regardless of size.
How do you resize EBS volume?	Modify → growpart → resize2fs.
Can you decrease EBS size?	❌ No, only increase.
How to copy snapshot to another region?	Actions → Copy Snapshot.
What is Recycle Bin for Snapshot?	Retains deleted snapshots for recovery.
Can you share EBS Snapshot?	Yes, across AWS accounts.
How do you automate EBS backups?	Use Lifecycle Manager.
What is Multi-Attach EBS?	io1/io2 volume accessible by multiple EC2s.
What is difference between Snapshot and AMI?	Snapshot = volume backup, AMI = full instance backup (includes root + metadata).
✅ 16. Summary

EBS = Persistent block storage

Snapshots = Incremental backups stored in S3

Lifecycle Manager = Automatic backup policy

gp3 = Best general-purpose SSD

io2 = For high-performance databases

Multi-Attach = For clustered apps

Encryption = Default best practice
